e Question 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nTina was a 10-year-old child. Her parents brought her to the doctor one day because she fell ill. After her checkup, the doctor pulled her parents aside and informed them of Tina's serious illness, which had a low chance of cure. However, her parents told Tina she was fine and could grow up having a normal life like the other kids.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Tina ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Pessimism\nB) Nervousness\nC) Hopeless\nD) Grief\nE) Hopeful\nF) Relief\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Tina feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) She realized her illness is not serious\nB) She realized her illness is very serious\nC) She realized her parents don't have to worry anymore\nD) She gets to get cured and go back to her normal life","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.02297736890645879,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e903d6006945d280b1a4","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369795292,"createTime":"2026-11-11 12:03:15","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"c980d59d6e9540ff94442ac961a64946"}